//RS 
//RS /// The sampling plan the TIR item walk records for every contract candidate:
//RS /// contract key → `None` (sampled: predicate + wrapper were materialized) or
//RS /// `Some(reason)` (explicit unavailable record; only the trivial unavailable
//RS /// wrapper was materialized).
//RS pub(super) type ContractSamplingPlan = BTreeMap<String, Option<String>>;
//RS 
//RS /// One canonical eligibility fact for generated contract sampling (#2502).
//RS ///
//RS /// Both artifact discovery and TIR item materialization consult this same
//RS /// classification, so every emitted test row resolves to a lowered callable
//RS /// and every non-sampled candidate is an explicit unavailable record — never
//RS /// an unresolved synthetic key and never silently omitted. `covered` is the
